  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nAn upper ridge over the western states will bring the heat back to\nthe area through the weekend. A weak frontal system will help to\nbring west winds Friday, Scattered storms are expected over\nsouthern Sask tonight and one could briefly flirt with the\nnorthern zones. Low chance pops are in place to cover that.\n\nAbundant smoke from the Pacific NW fires is expected to stream \ninto the area Friday and could knock visibility in some places to \njust 2 to 3 miles.\n\nWinds tomorrow across Fort Peck Lake could be strong enough for a\nLake Wind Advisory.\n\nWill upgrade the Extreme Heat Watch to a Warning for most\nlocations. Some in the northeast zones will have a Heat Advisory\nthat will last into Sunday.\n\nWill upgrade the Fire Weather Watch for Friday to a Red Flag\nWarning. Will not extend it into Saturday as winds do not look to\nbe strong enough. Fire weather issues may arise Sunday with higher\nwinds and low humidity. However zones 136 and 137 may not have the\nwind to reach the criteria.\n\nThe upper ridge next week tries to push east but an upper trough \nover the eastern US keeps it at bay. Expect a slight cooldown but\ntemps will remain above normal with mainly dry conditions.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nAdded thunderstorm chances to the forecast for tonight as some of\nthe CAMS are hinting at this. No other changes to NBM. \n\nLow confidence that there will be a thunderstorm somewhere in \nnortheast Montana tonight, based on HREF. High confidence on \nbreezy west winds on Friday and on the heat this weekend. \nTFJ",
